WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:10.549 align:start position:0%
 
a gun  over his shoulder and a kiss for a child  one of the key houthi rebel leaders  knows how to work a crowd  he and his armed guards are here to  rally the troops and remind the sparring  militant factions  who the real enemies are  death to america death to israel and the  west they're chanting  time and again the former head of the  houthi revolutionary council  urges the fighters to stay strong  the houthis have held out for five long  years  backed and funded by iran this  impoverished country is the pawn in the  middle of a proxy war  against a coalition headed by saudi  arabia and supported by britain  these people feel like they're taking on  some of the giants of the world  saudi arabia america even britain and  france and that's what's  uniting them all this suspicion and this  distrust  of those political powerhouses but the  rebels have been repeatedly accused by  the united  nations of committing war crimes too  there's a u.n report which says  that the houthis are recruiting children  as  soldiers is there any truth in this  the gun culture is strong here but he  denies forcing children into the  conflict  no no no these people you see all around  you  are they children the u.n  takes all their information from our  enemies  we've been given exclusive access to the  former houthi president  one of the commanders who helped the  rebels seize control of the yemeni  capital sana six years ago  he's now bent on accusing the coalition  of a litany of war crimes  and takes us to a bridge which he claims  has been bombed with the help of british  expertise  the british prime minister is aware of  all this he tells us  we drove hundreds of kilometers through  dry riverbeds  traversing remote and rocky mountain  trails  eventually climbing up the last few  hundred meters  to reach the isolated hillside village  community of washer  close to the saudi border we are the  first foreigners to reach here  the first outsiders to investigate this  attack and see what happened on the  ground  here an air strike wrought terrible  damage  reducing one home to rubble within  seconds  inside it was packed with women and  children from the majali family who were  gathering for lunch  nine people were killed instantly six of  them children  targeting civilian areas is an  international war crime  one of the neighbors holds up a baby's  bib pulled out of the debris  and leggings belonging to one of the  toddlers  there is household paraphernalia all  around solar panels a tv satellite dish  cooking equipment the attack shocked  this community  who've become so used to their cries of  injustice going unheard  of there were body parts  i've never seen anything like this  before  we found shrapnel from the bomb still  littering the site  and neighbors and relatives showed us  pictures they took immediately  afterwards  many of the dead children are too  graphic to show but there are also  photographs showing identifying marks on  the bomb  fragments we tracked other pictures  filmed soon after the attack by houthi  activists  and shrapnel collected by them it  appears to be the same  with the same markings weapons experts  we consulted told us the fragments found  here seem to be part of a  500-pound fin guided bomb manufactured  in america a coalition spokesman said  they were investigating whether this was  an  accidental loss of civilian life whilst  targeting houthi leaders and fighters  but this is a poor farming community no  adult men were amongst the dead or  injured  there were only three survivors from the  washer attack  and one of them is a baby we crisscross  the mountain paths again  and managed to track down all of them  the first fled to hajja city 130  kilometers away from washer  nora told us she was feeding her baby  boy when the missile  hit her two daughters were killed  somehow she and the baby survived  i was screaming for help i was in shock  she says the house was destroyed i was  searching for my daughter but she was  dead  then i saw my sister-in-law and she was  dead too i just picked up my son  and screamed for help the third survivor  is a young teenage boy who he traced to  his cousin's house on the outskirts of  sana  he has the scars but he can't remember  anything  his cousins can they pulled him out  barely alive and are still  traumatized by it  you only recognize his mother from her  torso  one of the small children from his face  it was his brother's son his arms were  cut off  and his sister-in-law she had no leg and  no arm and she was  totally burned he said he heard the  explosion  but whilst they were scrambling to find  survivors the same jets circled the area  for 15 minutes  terrifying them further  the largest independent human rights  group in yemen is compiling a dossier of  what they say  are war crimes on both sides they've  documented at least 500 coalition  attacks against schools  hospitals and other civilian areas and a  handful  directly linking british arms  manufacturers and suppliers to the  crimes  people who are in authority in uk and  could have stopped this uh from  happening that they they didn't  they should uh take their responsibility  and they should stand in front of court  right  next to the victims who were injured or  killed in this  the villages of russia have very little  but they want justice more than anything  and those responsible for these  atrocities held to account  alex crawford sky news in washer yemen

